STEP FUNCTIONS:
├── Retry logic         → Retry field (MaxAttempts, IntervalSeconds, BackoffRate)
├── Error handling      → Catch field → fallback state
├── Long-running tasks  → Set TimeoutSeconds generously
├── Trigger from S3     → EventBridge → Step Functions (DIRECT)
└── Activity tasks      → External/human workflows only

GLUE JOB TROUBLESHOOTING:
├── OOM / "killed by YARN"        → Increase worker memory (G.2X, G.4X)
├── Job slow (constant data)      → Check DPUs, partitioning, data skew
├── Gradually increasing runtime  → Job Bookmarks broken (reprocessing!)
├── Streaming not processing      → Checkpoint stuck / retention expired
└── Small files on read           → groupFiles + groupSize

MONITORING & ALERTING:
├── Detect job FAILURE    → EventBridge state change event → SNS
├── Detect slow jobs      → CloudWatch metric alarm on duration
├── Detect missing data   → EventBridge + metric alarm on zero events
└── Data quality checks   → Glue Data Quality (DQDL rules)

AIRFLOW (MWAA):
├── Trigger Glue job      → AwsGlueJobOperator (native, auto-polls)
├── Retry failed tasks    → "Clear" task instance
├── Connection issues     → Check security group outbound rules
└── Always prefer native AWS operators over Bash/Python+boto3

EVENTBRIDGE DIRECT TARGETS (no Lambda needed):
├── Step Functions ✅
├── SNS ✅
├── SQS ✅
├── Lambda ✅
├── Glue Workflows ✅
└── Kinesis Data Streams ✅

MONITORING — "LEAST EFFORT" ANSWERS:
├── Detect missing data (real-time)  → EventBridge + CloudWatch metric + alarm
├── S3 Storage Lens                  → Daily aggregate analytics only (NOT real-time)
├── Centralized job monitoring       → Glue console built-in insights (already exists!)
└── Don't over-engineer when native tools exist

STEP FUNCTIONS PATTERNS:
├── .sync         → Wait for job to complete
├── .waitForTaskToken → Wait for external callback
├── Retry         → Automatic retries with backoff
├── Catch         → Error handling → fallback state
├── Parallel      → Waits for ALL branches before proceeding
└── Redrive       → Re-execute failed execution from point of failure


